<section class="container" style="padding-block:4rem 2rem;max-width:760px;">
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">After acquiring Bankverein Werther, Volksbank Paderborn-Höxter-Detmold faced a decision that in bank acquisitions is regularly made too quickly in favour of a single brand: Bankverein Werther remained in the market as an independent brand — endorsed by Volksbank PHD, not dissolved into it.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Unlike a relaunch born of strategic necessity (as at Cobiax or Arminia), the point here was not to correct a weak form but to deliberately preserve an intact form that people trusted locally — while making it regionally connectable for a much larger catchment area.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:900px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Change follows strategy: preserving instead of dissolving</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Here the strategic analysis produced perhaps the purest form of the principle: the existing form did not need to change at all. Bankverein Werther carries real, long-grown trust locally — dissolving it just to create a more uniform brand picture would have cost more than it brought. The answer was an endorsement: belonging to the larger, more stable Volksbank PHD is made visible without replacing the local identity.</p>

  <div class="compare-grid reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
    <div class="compare-col">
      <span class="compare-tag">Before the acquisition</span>
      <div class="case-img case-img--square case-img--logo" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
        <img src="/img/Bankverein_Werther_logo_alt.svg" alt="Bankverein Werther — brand mark before integration">
      </div>
      <p class="compare-text">The long-established local brand. It carried the trust of generations of customers — and for exactly that reason was no candidate for dissolution.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-col">
      <span class="compare-tag">After integration</span>
      <div class="case-img case-img--square case-img--logo" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
        <img src="/img/Bankverein_Werther_logo_neu.svg" alt="Bankverein Werther — brand mark endorsed by Volksbank Paderborn-Höxter-Detmold">
      </div>
      <p class="compare-text">The same brand, with visible membership of the cooperative group added. The local connection remains the sender; size becomes additional security.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 3rem;max-width:900px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Two senders, one brand architecture</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">At its core, brand architecture is a decision about who speaks to the customer. In the endorsement model, the local brand remains the sender, while the umbrella brand vouches for creditworthiness, reach and range of services — a constellation that in the cooperative banking sector is closer to reality anyway than a full merger.</p>
  <div class="grid-3 reveal reveal-delay-1" style="align-items:center;">
    <div class="case-img case-img--square case-img--logo" style="max-width:240px;margin:0 auto;">
      <img src="/img/Logos-pur/Volksbank.svg" alt="Volksbank Paderborn-Höxter-Detmold — brand mark of the umbrella brand">
    </div>
    <div class="case-img case-img--square case-img--logo" style="max-width:240px;margin:0 auto;">
      <img src="/img/Logos-pur/Bankverein-Werther.svg" alt="Bankverein Werther — brand mark of the retained local brand">
    </div>
    <p class="compare-text">Left, the umbrella brand that stands for stability and range of services. Right, the retained local brand that continues to speak in customer contact. The economic value of the acquisition lay precisely in not playing the two off against each other.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 3rem;max-width:760px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">“Wir sprechen teuto.”</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">For Volksbank PHD itself — with a much larger catchment area after the acquisition — regionality became the unifying principle of its direction. The slogan “Wir sprechen teuto.” (“We speak Teuto.”) carries belonging to the Teutoburg Forest region directly in its wording — understandable, warm, unmistakably regional, yet viable for the entire new area, not just a single location.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-1">What was advertised was not the acquisition, but the shared regional belonging that already existed before it.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:0 3rem;max-width:1100px;">
  <figure class="reveal" style="margin:0;">
    <div class="case-img" style="aspect-ratio:16/9;">
      {% respImage "img/Teutoburger-Wald.jpg", "View across the Teutoburg Forest to the plain beyond with its settlements", "(min-width: 1100px) 1100px, 100vw" %}
    </div>
    <figcaption style="font-size:.75rem;color:rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.5);margin-top:.6rem;line-height:1.5;">The Teutoburg Forest: not a location, but the common denominator of a catchment area that carried three names after the acquisition.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="max-width:760px;margin:2rem auto 0;">A slogan that names one town excludes the others. “Wir sprechen teuto.” names instead the landscape everyone shares in — and is therefore equally viable for Paderborn, Höxter and Detmold without becoming arbitrary. Regionality without rivalry between locations.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:760px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">What has happened since</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">On 1 December 2011, Volksbank Paderborn-Höxter-Detmold took over the core business of Bankverein Werther, including the brand. In 2017 it merged itself with Volksbank Minden and has since been called VerbundVolksbank OWL.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">This proves something that could otherwise only be claimed: <strong>the local brand has outlived the name of the bank that acquired it.</strong> The building in the picture above still reads “Bankverein Werther” — and below it, smaller, the addition of the umbrella brand, now in its third version. That is exactly how the endorsement model was intended: the sender stays, the roof above it may change.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2">A merger would have written off this value in 2011 — and caused adjustment costs a second time in 2017.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:900px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Targeted instead of scattered</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">A larger catchment area also means more heterogeneous customer groups. The target-group approach of Volksbank PHD was therefore defined using the Sinus-Milieus — an established, empirically grounded model for describing values and lifestyles — instead of rough demographic assumptions. This made genuinely targeted communication possible across different customer segments, not just communication that felt right.</p>
</section>

